Error [E0320]: struct construction uses `Stats{…}`, not `Stats.{…}`
  --> tests/ui/computed_field_set.jet:8:16
    |
  8 |     s := Stats.{strength: 10, attack: 5}
    |                ^
 Why: literal heads place no dot before their brace (D-LIT-DOT1)
 Fix: write `Stats{…}`

Error [E0339]: `attack` is a computed field on `Stats` — it can't be set
  --> tests/ui/computed_field_set.jet:8:31
    |
  8 |     s := Stats.{strength: 10, attack: 5}
    |                               ^^^^^^
 Why: `attack` is declared `attack => …` — its value always comes from that formula, never from a struct literal
 Fix: remove `attack` from this `.{ … }`
